  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, establishing RNA as the dominant signal, while config_010 (image-only, resnet50) achieves only 20.8%, indicating the image modality is currently a weak or uninformative source. This leaves the RNA-side design choices as the highest-leverage area to explore. Question: config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly tests whether moving from a single profile to multiple profiles with average-pool aggregation improves RNA classification, while holding the encoder (pca_n2000) constant. This isolates the profile/aggregation effect in a clean A/B comparison against config_001. Why this is the best next step: Under a tight budget, understanding whether multiprofile aggregation adds value over singleprofile is a prerequisite for interpreting all downstream multimodal and multiprofile configurations (configs 018-051). If multiprofile does not help the RNA baseline, many complex configurations can be deprioritized; if it does, we gain a strong prior for which aggregation strategies to pair with fusion. This single experiment reduces the most uncertainty about a design axis that affects the majority of remaining configurations."
}

